-- mod-stellar-tarot — the spells the client must know.
--
-- Two spells do nothing: 88000 sits on every card and 88001 on every board,
-- so that the client lets the player USE the item -- a client sends nothing
-- for a spell it has no row for. The module intercepts the use server side
-- (ITEM_EVENT_ON_USE, in the Lua interface) and relays it to `.tarot study`,
-- which does the work; the cast never happens.
--
-- 88002 is the BANNER: the one aura the player sees while any effect is in
-- force; its text points at the window. The others are the TEST AURAS of the
-- cards: 88000 + 4 x card + (level - 1), one statistic each, +1234 --
-- placeholders until the powers are designed -- hidden from the aura bar
-- (AttributesEx 0x10000000, SPELL_ATTR1_NO_AURA_ICON) so that only the
-- banner shows. A card may name any spell instead, the game's own included.
--
-- The server reads these rows from `spell_dbc`; the client from
-- data/dbc/stellartarot_Spell.dbc, merged into its own file by the installer.
-- Both are written from the same source.
--
-- THE LANGUAGE COLUMN. A text block counts sixteen slots, and the client's
-- order is 0 enUS, 1 koKR, 2 frFR, 3 deDE... The columns of `spell_dbc` name
-- one more, `_Lang_enGB` at 1, and slide by one from there: the column holding
-- FRENCH is called `_Lang_koKR`, and the one called `_Lang_frFR` is German.
--
-- GENERATED by the author's tooling. Regenerable.

DELETE FROM `spell_dbc` WHERE `ID` BETWEEN 87000 AND 89999;
